Upstream (zbirenbaum/copilot-cmp, unmaintained -- this is HEAD) calls the
client field `self.client.is_stopped()` with a DOT. In Neovim 0.11+ the dotted
`client.is_stopped` field is a deprecation shim over the `client:is_stopped()`
method, so every call emits

    client.is_stopped is deprecated. Run ":checkhealth vim.deprecated" ...

source.is_available() runs on essentially every completion request, and copilot
attaches to every buffer, so this was the single noisiest line in :messages.

Switching the dot to a colon calls the real method. Behaviour is identical --
the shim just forwards to it.

The `not self.client.name == "copilot"` on the same line is a separate upstream
bug (it parses as `(not self.client.name) == "copilot"`, always false) and is
deliberately left alone: fixing it would change which sources are offered.

--- a/lua/copilot_cmp/source.lua
+++ b/lua/copilot_cmp/source.lua
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ end
 
 source.is_available = function(self)
   -- client is stopped.
-  if self.client.is_stopped() or not self.client.name == "copilot" then
+  if self.client:is_stopped() or not self.client.name == "copilot" then
     return false
   end
 
